Building the package
====================

libcosmic and its dependencies aren't in Debian, so the package builds offline
from a vendor tree. Create it once, with network:

    cargo vendor debian/vendor

debian/rules points cargo at it with --config debian/cargo-vendor.toml. If
cargo vendor prints a different [source.*] block (a git source changed in
Cargo.lock), update that file. The vendor tree is large and not committed.

Then:

    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

libwayland-client0 is loaded with dlopen, so it is listed by hand in Depends.
The app is Wayland only and draws on the CPU, so it needs no X11 or GPU
libraries. The file chooser and the About page's links go through
xdg-desktop-portal (Depends), with xdg-desktop-portal-cosmic on COSMIC
(Recommends). No fc-cache is needed: fontconfig notices new files by the
directory's mtime.
